479 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Long before there was a Lynn's Table in Old Town Spring, there were two young chefs who met in culinary school. This year Matthew and Jessica are celebrating 30 years of marriage and 11 years in business, and if you stop in on any given day, you'll find them both there. Matthew is usually in the kitchen or stepping out to visit with a table. Jessica is somewhere between the dessert case, the dining room and the hundred other things that come with owning an independent restaurant.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
481 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (Here's the part of Jessica's story we love. She grew up quiet and shy, and never imagined she'd become the public voice of a restaurant. Somewhere along the way she found that voice, and discovered that making people feel welcome and cared for is one of the things that brings her the most joy. You feel that the minute you walk in.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E (It's also why they chose the words they did for their motto: Make yourself at home. For Matthew and Jessica, that isn't a slogan on the wall. They point to where the word restaurant comes from, the French restaurer, which means to restore or refresh. They want Lynn's Table to be the place you step away from your day, settle in, eat something wonderful and leave feeling a little better than when you came. As Matthew puts it:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 237 0 R
/E ("From our kitchen to your table, every dish is prepared to nourish your body and lift your spirits. Relax, indulge, and allow us to restore you.")
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
