490 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (Some of that feeling comes straight from their own family tables. The Spaghetti Bolognese is Matthew's mother's recipe, and Grandma Pat's Pimento Cheese has become a Lynn's Table favorite in its own right. There's something special about a dish that once fed one family now feeding yours.)
/E (Some of that feeling comes straight from their own family tables. The Spaghetti Bolognese is Matthew's mother's recipe, and Grandma Pat's Pimento Cheese has become a Lynn's Table favorite in its own right. There's something special about a dish that once fed one family now feeding yours.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
491 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 238 0 R
/T (Elevated comfort food, thoughtfully crafted)
/E (Elevated comfort food, thoughtfully crafted)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
492 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (That's how Matthew and Jessica describe their food, and they're quick to say what "elevated" doesn't mean. It doesn't mean complicated, fussy or pretentious. It means paying attention: good ingredients, real technique and care in every step.)
/E (That's how Matthew and Jessica describe their food, and they're quick to say what "elevated" doesn't mean. It doesn't mean complicated, fussy or pretentious. It means paying attention: good ingredients, real technique and care in every step.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (You can see it in what they choose to cook with. The beef is Texas HeartBrand Akaushi. The bread comes from Kraftsmen Baking right here in Houston. The ice cream is Tillamook. And there's something you won't find in their kitchen at all: a conventional deep fryer. Take the Chicken Fried Steak, which is about as Texas comfort food as it gets. At Lynn's Table it starts with beef tenderloin, gets hand-breaded, then shallow-fried in beef tallow. Same dish you grew up on, made the way a classically trained chef would make it.)
/E (You can see it in what they choose to cook with. The beef is Texas HeartBrand Akaushi. The bread comes from Kraftsmen Baking right here in Houston. The ice cream is Tillamook. And there's something you won't find in their kitchen at all: a conventional deep fryer. Take the Chicken Fried Steak, which is about as Texas comfort food as it gets. At Lynn's Table it starts with beef tenderloin, gets hand-breaded, then shallow-fried in beef tallow. Same dish you grew up on, made the way a classically trained chef would make it.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (That's really Matthew's gift. Forty years of training doesn't show up as food you need a dictionary to order. It shows up as a burger or a chicken fried steak that's simply better than you expected. The same hands that turn out a beautifully prepared Beef Tournedos or Filet Oscar are the ones breading that steak, and the same care goes into both. An Akaushi burger and a chef's special sit comfortably on the same menu, because to Matthew they deserve the same attention. Serious technique, without taking the fun out of comfort food.)
/E (That's really Matthew's gift. Forty years of training doesn't show up as food you need a dictionary to order. It shows up as a burger or a chicken fried steak that's simply better than you expected. The same hands that turn out a beautifully prepared Beef Tournedos or Filet Oscar are the ones breading that steak, and the same care goes into both. An Akaushi burger and a chef's special sit comfortably on the same menu, because to Matthew they deserve the same attention. Serious technique, without taking the fun out of comfort food.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (If you only know Lynn's Table as a lunch spot or a sandwich stop during an afternoon of shopping, dinner is where all of this really comes alive. There's a weekly rhythm you can plan around: that tenderloin Chicken Fried Steak, slow-roasted Prime Rib, All-You-Can-Eat Spaghetti Bolognese and Lobster Friday. Then there are Matthew's rotating specials, which have included Lobster & Jumbo Lump Crab Cakes, New Orleans-style BBQ Shrimp, schnitzel, gnocchi, Beef Tournedos and Filet Oscar. The menu you see this month may have something entirely new on it the next.)
/E (If you only know Lynn's Table as a lunch spot or a sandwich stop during an afternoon of shopping, dinner is where all of this really comes alive. There's a weekly rhythm you can plan around: that tenderloin Chicken Fried Steak, slow-roasted Prime Rib, All-You-Can-Eat Spaghetti Bolognese and Lobster Friday. Then there are Matthew's rotating specials, which have included Lobster & Jumbo Lump Crab Cakes, New Orleans-style BBQ Shrimp, schnitzel, gnocchi, Beef Tournedos and Filet Oscar. The menu you see this month may have something entirely new on it the next.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (And please, save room. Dessert is Jessica's side of the table: cakes, pies, bread pudding, plus sundaes, milkshakes, malts and floats made with that Tillamook ice cream. Her latest love is the house-made fudge, and with the holidays coming she's working on seasonal flavors and gift selections made for sharing. If there's someone on your list who's hard to shop for, consider this your hint.)
/E (And please, save room. Dessert is Jessica's side of the table: cakes, pies, bread pudding, plus sundaes, milkshakes, malts and floats made with that Tillamook ice cream. Her latest love is the house-made fudge, and with the holidays coming she's working on seasonal flavors and gift selections made for sharing. If there's someone on your list who's hard to shop for, consider this your hint.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
497 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 238 0 R
/T (After 11 years, Matthew and Jessica know a lot of their guests by name. Their tables have hosted birthdays, anniversaries, date nights and long lunches with friends. Their favorite compliment? When someone discovers Lynn's Table and comes back with somebody they want to introduce to it. We'd love for you to be that someone this month.)
/E (After 11 years, Matthew and Jessica know a lot of their guests by name. Their tables have hosted birthdays, anniversaries, date nights and long lunches with friends. Their favorite compliment? When someone discovers Lynn's Table and comes back with somebody they want to introduce to it. We'd love for you to be that someone this month.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
