/Title (That's really Matthew's gift. Forty years of training doesn't show up as food you need a dictionary to order. It shows up as a burger or a chicken fried steak that's simply better than you expected. The same hands that turn out a beautifully prepared Beef Tournedos or Filet Oscar are the ones breading that steak, and the same care goes into both. An Akaushi burger and a chef's special sit comfortably on the same menu, because to Matthew they deserve the same attention. Serious technique, without taking the fun out of comfort food.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1143 0 R
/Prev 1342 0 R
/Next 1393 0 R
>>
endobj
1392 0 obj
<<
/Title (And please, save room. Dessert is Jessica's side of the table: cakes, pies, bread pudding, plus sundaes, milkshakes, malts and floats made with that Tillamook ice cream. Her latest love is the house-made fudge, and with the holidays coming she's working on seasonal flavors and gift selections made for sharing. If there's someone on your list who's hard to shop for, consider this your hint.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1143 0 R
/Prev 1393 0 R
/Next 1343 0 R
>>
endobj
1393 0 obj
<<
/Title (If you only know Lynn's Table as a lunch spot or a sandwich stop during an afternoon of shopping, dinner is where all of this really comes alive. There's a weekly rhythm you can plan around: that tenderloin Chicken Fried Steak, slow-roasted Prime Rib, All-You-Can-Eat Spaghetti Bolognese and Lobster Friday. Then there are Matthew's rotating specials, which have included Lobster & Jumbo Lump Crab Cakes, New Orleans-style BBQ Shrimp, schnitzel, gnocchi, Beef Tournedos and Filet Oscar. The menu you see this month may have something entirely new on it the next.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1143 0 R
/Prev 1391 0 R
/Next 1392 0 R
>>
endobj
